1
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:40,240
=Ren Yu=

2
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,000
(Adapted from Lei Mi's novel Ren Yu)

3
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
=Episode 9=

4
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,719
Don't wander off.

5
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,239
Mommy's right here.

6
00:02:07,599 --> 00:02:08,520
Be careful.

7
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:12,879
I see you.

8
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,919
I'm coming.

9
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,680
(What color are your dreams?)

10
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,400
My girl's all grown up.

11
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,960
She's even learning to save.

12
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:01,560
Brilliant.

13
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,599
Brilliant.

14
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:08,840
How's that spelled?

15
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,280
It's a spelling test. Focus.

16
00:03:12,599 --> 00:03:13,919
Come on. Brilliant.

17
00:03:18,759 --> 00:03:20,439
(What color is the world)

18
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,159
(after you wake up?)

19
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:47,879
The doctor said your leg

20
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,639
won't ever be the same.

21
00:03:51,719 --> 00:03:53,240
But if it heals well,

22
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,000
you should still be able to walk.

23
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,240
Once you're discharged,

24
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:00,879
you can work as my doorman.

25
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,800
Same pay.

26
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,080
As long as I'm alive,

27
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:05,879
I'll take care of you.

28
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,240
I'll cover your son's tuition too.

29
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,719
I've contacted someone

30
00:04:11,759 --> 00:04:12,879
about Su Lin's death certificate.

31
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,079
She's gone. That's the truth.

32
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,439
Thinking won't change it.

33
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:32,600
Let's focus on the life ahead.

34
00:04:33,519 --> 00:04:34,319
Get some rest.

35
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,720
You should've let me die.

36
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:50,279
I'm not heartless enough to let you die.

37
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,240
(My leg is ruined.)

38
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,079
(But my family must survive.)

39
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:23,839
(Lin,)

40
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,040
(I'm sorry. I have no choice.)

41
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,680
Mr. Ma, this is a school.

42
00:05:31,839 --> 00:05:32,879
We can't accept gifts.

43
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:34,240
I understand.

44
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:36,439
I bought an extra one last time.

45
00:05:36,759 --> 00:05:38,439
I thought you might need one,

46
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,360
so I brought it over.

47
00:05:40,879 --> 00:05:42,639
We're friends, after all.

48
00:05:43,839 --> 00:05:44,959
I asked you here today

49
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,480
to talk about your daughter.

50
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,879
Na's caused trouble again?

51
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,199
Ma Na

52
00:06:00,319 --> 00:06:01,959
has a strong personality.

53
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,319
At school,

54
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:05,439
she often clashes with classmates.

55
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,240
Kids roughhousing

56
00:06:07,279 --> 00:06:09,000
is perfectly normal.

57
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:10,959
But recently,

58
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,639
something happened.

59
00:06:13,439 --> 00:06:15,720
I wanted our school to do well

60
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,639
in the contest.

61
00:06:16,879 --> 00:06:19,600
so I hired Mr. Zhou from Culture Center

62
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:20,959
to coach the team.

63
00:06:21,439 --> 00:06:25,079
Ma Na insulted him.

64
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,360
But that's not the worst part.

65
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,120
The worst part is,

66
00:06:28,759 --> 00:06:30,120
Mr. Zhou's father-in-law

67
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,720
is a city cultural official.

68
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,160
I've spoiled her rotten.

69
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:40,279
Mr. Ma,

70
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,120
let's be fair.

71
00:06:42,439 --> 00:06:43,639
It doesn't matter who he is.

72
00:06:43,639 --> 00:06:45,000
Insulting him was wrong.

73
00:06:45,639 --> 00:06:46,160
Yes.

74
00:06:46,639 --> 00:06:47,879
So what I'm suggesting

75
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,360
is that Ma Na

76
00:06:49,519 --> 00:06:51,480
apologize to Mr. Zhou.

77
00:06:51,759 --> 00:06:52,879
Then we can move past this.

78
00:06:53,519 --> 00:06:54,439
Absolutely.

79
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:55,839
I'll handle it today.

80
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:08,160
Your tape has much better songs.

81
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:10,240
My dad's

82
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,120
is half disco.

83
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,199
I wish Mom would buy me a Walkman.

84
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,600
Use mine for now.

85
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,519
You can borrow my tapes too.

86
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,600
Your folks will see

87
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,040
how hard you're studying English,

88
00:07:20,199 --> 00:07:21,199
and they'll buy you one soon.

89
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,120
What's got you so happy?

90
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:24,319
What is it?

91
00:07:24,399 --> 00:07:25,199
Let me see.

92
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,600
I haven't heard this tape either.

93
00:07:29,879 --> 00:07:30,439
Jiang Ting,

94
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,279
you're so sweet.

95
00:07:31,319 --> 00:07:32,199
Let me borrow it too.

96
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,439
Jiang Ting,

97
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,720
let's see what else

98
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,120
you've got in your bag.

99
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:42,920
Give it to me.

100
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,319
Good things are meant to be shared.

101
00:07:49,519 --> 00:07:50,240
What?

102
00:08:03,639 --> 00:08:05,000
Jiang Ting, come out!

103
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,040
Hiding won't get you off the hook.

104
00:08:09,959 --> 00:08:11,480
Let's see how long you last.

105
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:14,480
Jiang Ting!

106
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,519
Come out!

107
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:19,399
Ma Na?

108
00:08:24,439 --> 00:08:24,920
Listen.

109
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:27,279
I'll lure her away.

110
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,279
Jiang Ting,

111
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:29,279
after that,

112
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,160
will you tell me everything

113
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,559
you know about Su Lin?

114
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,600
Stop hiding and come out!

115
00:08:34,759 --> 00:08:35,559
Come out!

116
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,120
Why do you need to know about Su Lin?

117
00:08:38,639 --> 00:08:39,919
I'll explain later.

118
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,679
I'll go.

119
00:08:41,879 --> 00:08:42,679
Stay hidden for now.

120
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,279
What are you doing in there?

121
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,080
Where's Jiang Ting?

122
00:08:53,159 --> 00:08:53,799
Come with me.

123
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:56,000
What are you doing? Let go!

124
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,840
Let go!

125
00:08:59,879 --> 00:09:00,360
Let go!

126
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,440
You're helping Jiang Ting, aren't you?

127
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:04,960
That's right.

128
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:08,159
I'm sick of you bullying people.

129
00:09:08,639 --> 00:09:11,000
Jiang Ting acts weak and innocent,

130
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,320
then finds every way she can

131
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,600
to make people like her.

132
00:09:13,799 --> 00:09:15,480
You and those other fools

133
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,879
all fell for it.

134
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,679
All over one cheap tape.

135
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:19,720
How pathetic.

136
00:09:20,639 --> 00:09:21,080
So?

137
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,279
What?

138
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,320
What's wrong with

139
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,360
wanting to be popular?

140
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,000
At least to me,

141
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,399
being liked is better

142
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,799
than being hated.

143
00:09:33,879 --> 00:09:34,480
But you

144
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,600
pretend you don't care,

145
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:37,960
like nothing bothers you.

146
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,120
Then you get jealous

147
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:40,679
and turn others against her.

148
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,600
What's the point?

149
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:42,679
Exactly.

150
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,240
So answer me this.

151
00:09:44,919 --> 00:09:45,720
Do you like me?

152
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,120
No.

153
00:09:49,559 --> 00:09:51,080
You really like Jiang Ting?

154
00:09:51,639 --> 00:09:52,559
Ma Na, listen.

155
00:09:53,399 --> 00:09:54,440
There's more to life

156
00:09:54,559 --> 00:09:56,639
than liking or disliking someone.

157
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:59,000
And just because I don't like you

158
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,639
doesn't mean I like someone else.

159
00:10:01,399 --> 00:10:02,720
You don't really like me.

160
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,200
You just hate being rejected,

161
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,879
so now you have to win.

162
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:08,639
And right now,

163
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:10,879
none of this matters.

164
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,759
Who cares that?

165
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,440
I always get what I want.

166
00:10:16,519 --> 00:10:17,200
Ma Na!

167
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,480
I've been looking everywhere.

168
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:20,919
The teacher wants you

169
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,879
in the lobby downstairs.

170
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:22,960
Your dad's here.

171
00:10:23,759 --> 00:10:25,240
You're nothing but trouble.

172
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,759
Ma Na.

173
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,559
Come in. Have a seat.

174
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,159
Get up!

175
00:10:47,679 --> 00:10:49,159
What did I do?

176
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:50,720
Have you forgotten basic manners?

177
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,639
You ask permission at the door.

178
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,879
Wait to be invited in.

179
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:55,000
He's still standing.

180
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:55,799
Why are you sitting?

181
00:10:55,879 --> 00:10:56,919
You're mad over that?

182
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,600
Are you out of your mind?

183
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,759
Principal Dong told me to sit.

184
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:03,000
I can't ignore a teacher.

185
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,399
Mr. Ma.

186
00:11:05,639 --> 00:11:07,000
Over that?

187
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,200
You're a student.

188
00:11:09,639 --> 00:11:11,080
You skip class and neglect school,

189
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,039
bully your classmates,

190
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,919
and now you hit a teacher?

191
00:11:14,039 --> 00:11:15,159
I never hit anyone!

192
00:11:15,159 --> 00:11:16,240
You can't insult him either.

193
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,159
I didn't insult him.

194
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,279
I only told the truth.

195
00:11:18,279 --> 00:11:19,120
Enough. Stop arguing.

196
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,200
Calm down, Mr. Ma.

197
00:11:20,399 --> 00:11:21,320
Mr. Zhou is here.

198
00:11:21,399 --> 00:11:22,399
Keep it together.

199
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,799
Apologize to Mr. Zhou.

200
00:11:30,879 --> 00:11:31,919
Do you hear me?

201
00:11:31,919 --> 00:11:32,799
No, don't hit her.

202
00:11:32,799 --> 00:11:33,080
I...

203
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:33,639
Principal Dong.

204
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:35,879
Mr. Zhou, come in.

205
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:36,600
Please.

206
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,840
Let me introduce you.

207
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,759
This is Mr. Zhou.

208
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,159
This is Ma Na's father.

209
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,360
He insisted on apologizing.

210
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,120
Hello.

211
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,279
Mr. Zhou, I'm so sorry.

212
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,320
My daughter is out of control.

213
00:11:49,519 --> 00:11:51,039
I was just punishing her.

214
00:11:51,039 --> 00:11:52,320
Please don't hit her.

215
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,519
Kids make mistakes.

216
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,759
She needs more attention, not force.

217
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,720
You're right.

218
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:58,879
This is my fault.

219
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,799
Her mother died when she was young.

220
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,120
I run a business and raise her alone.

221
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,960
I honestly don't know what to do.

222
00:12:07,039 --> 00:12:07,720
I understand.

223
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,279
The school will work with you

224
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,759
to help her grow.

225
00:12:12,159 --> 00:12:12,960
Mr. Zhou

226
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,600
is excellent at spotting problems.

227
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,120
- He's impressive.
- Absolutely.

228
00:12:16,519 --> 00:12:17,080
Come here.

229
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,879
Apologize to Mr. Zhou.

230
00:12:23,279 --> 00:12:24,279
- That's not necessary.
- Sorry.

231
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:26,440
Don't hit her.

232
00:12:26,639 --> 00:12:27,240
Speak properly.

233
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,159
It's all right, Mr. Ma.

234
00:12:28,159 --> 00:12:29,039
No. Say it properly.

235
00:12:32,399 --> 00:12:33,360
Mr. Zhou,

236
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:36,399
I shouldn't have
said those things in public.

237
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,360
I was wrong. I'm sorry.

238
00:12:42,759 --> 00:12:44,360
That's enough.

239
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,279
And Mr. Zhou,

240
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:53,440
please accept this.

241
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,679
I really can't.

242
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:55,840
If you refuse,

243
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:56,919
then you haven't forgiven us.

244
00:12:56,919 --> 00:12:57,519
That's separate.

245
00:12:57,519 --> 00:12:58,200
Mr. Ma, please.

246
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:58,919
I forgive her.

247
00:12:58,919 --> 00:13:00,440
But schools can't accept gifts.

248
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,279
Don't pressure Mr. Zhou.

249
00:13:02,559 --> 00:13:04,480
Dad, your gift is so tacky.

250
00:13:05,919 --> 00:13:07,840
I have a tape here.

251
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:08,919
You can have it.

252
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:09,960
It's in English.

253
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:12,000
Mr. Zhou won't want that.

254
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,159
This is a good tape.

255
00:13:17,039 --> 00:13:17,759
For learning English,

256
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:19,480
songs are a great tool.

257
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,480
You can take it back

258
00:13:21,519 --> 00:13:22,480
whenever you want.

259
00:13:23,159 --> 00:13:24,840
Your daughter's clearly

260
00:13:24,879 --> 00:13:25,720
a self-motivated learner.

261
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,000
Sorry about the mess.

262
00:13:32,799 --> 00:13:34,120
I just got back from a trip.

263
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:35,759
The place is a wreck.

264
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,559
Clear yourselves a spot.

265
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:39,440
No problem.

266
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:41,279
One of my fish is about to give birth.

267
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,960
- I need to handle it.
- Okay.

268
00:13:43,679 --> 00:13:46,600
The male had already died.

269
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,320
Good thing I noticed in time

270
00:13:48,559 --> 00:13:49,600
and separated

271
00:13:49,919 --> 00:13:51,440
the pregnant female.

272
00:13:53,879 --> 00:13:54,639
Otherwise,

273
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,879
the fry would've been eaten

274
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,840
as soon as they were born.

275
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:01,480
Fish eat each other?

276
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,279
That's sick.

277
00:14:02,559 --> 00:14:03,879
It seems sick to you.

278
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,799
But among fish,

279
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,399
it's perfectly normal.

280
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,960
Just like the killer you're hunting.

281
00:14:10,919 --> 00:14:13,159
An ordinary person can't understand

282
00:14:13,159 --> 00:14:14,679
why he kills.

283
00:14:15,639 --> 00:14:16,879
But to him,

284
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,639
it may feel unavoidable.

285
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:22,720
That's exactly why

286
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,039
we came to consult you.

287
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,360
You're an expert in criminal psychology.

288
00:14:26,639 --> 00:14:28,919
What kind of person

289
00:14:29,039 --> 00:14:30,879
do you think the killer is?

290
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:33,519
Professor Qiao,

291
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,519
we have some theories,

292
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:36,840
but they contain

293
00:14:37,559 --> 00:14:39,000
a lot of contradictions.

294
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,519
All the victims were women.

295
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,279
They were sexually assaulted,

296
00:14:48,919 --> 00:14:51,879
then strangled with wire.

297
00:14:52,279 --> 00:14:55,759
They were stripped of
clothes and belongings

298
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:58,759
and dumped in underground pipes.

299
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:02,200
First, the killer likely had

300
00:15:02,519 --> 00:15:04,879
no obvious personal ties to them.

301
00:15:05,039 --> 00:15:07,960
Otherwise, we'd find him quickly.

302
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,360
You were right not to waste time

303
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,440
on the victims' social circles.

304
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,320
That's correct.

305
00:15:14,799 --> 00:15:16,200
So we believe

306
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:18,519
he approached each victim

307
00:15:18,759 --> 00:15:21,120
as a complete stranger,

308
00:15:21,279 --> 00:15:23,279
then took her somewhere

309
00:15:23,279 --> 00:15:24,440
suitable for the crime.

310
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,279
That suggests

311
00:15:28,279 --> 00:15:30,360
he doesn't seem threatening.

312
00:15:30,399 --> 00:15:30,919
Right?

313
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,679
He must at least

314
00:15:32,879 --> 00:15:36,000
look trustworthy.

315
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:41,000
He's probably 30 to 40 years old

316
00:15:42,039 --> 00:15:43,639
and likely has

317
00:15:43,679 --> 00:15:45,440
a respectable job.

318
00:15:45,759 --> 00:15:47,799
The victims were not wealthy enough

319
00:15:48,039 --> 00:15:49,840
to give him

320
00:15:50,039 --> 00:15:52,360
a financial motive.

321
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,240
So his motive

322
00:15:55,679 --> 00:15:58,440
was likely sexual gratification.

323
00:16:02,639 --> 00:16:04,159
From your description,

324
00:16:04,879 --> 00:16:07,240
he has opportunities to meet women.

325
00:16:07,919 --> 00:16:09,440
So he should have

326
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:11,399
other sexual outlets.

327
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:13,720
That's an internal issue.

328
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,600
Let's start with what we can observe.

329
00:16:17,159 --> 00:16:19,440
The rapes and murders

330
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:21,000
likely occurred indoors.

331
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,480
That suggests he lives alone.

332
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,000
And is single.

333
00:16:27,399 --> 00:16:28,519
That means...

334
00:16:28,799 --> 00:16:31,600
We can make another hypothesis.

335
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,200
It isn't certain,

336
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:37,679
but he may have another residence.

337
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,000
A temporary one,

338
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,120
where he lives a different life.

339
00:16:41,759 --> 00:16:42,799
You believe

340
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:45,000
he may have dumped all three bodies

341
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,039
in the same storm drain.

342
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,200
I agree.

343
00:16:50,279 --> 00:16:51,519
Which raises another question.

344
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:53,039
Why would he do that?

345
00:16:54,759 --> 00:16:55,759
Habit, perhaps.

346
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:58,679
Storm drains are regularly inspected

347
00:16:58,919 --> 00:16:59,720
and cleared.

348
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,759
If someone

349
00:17:00,799 --> 00:17:03,000
happened to open that manhole,

350
00:17:03,159 --> 00:17:05,680
his crimes would be exposed.

351
00:17:06,319 --> 00:17:08,079
You mean

352
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,960
he hides the bodies

353
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,559
at one specific spot in the system?

354
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:14,839
Possibly.

355
00:17:15,359 --> 00:17:17,799
Let's consider a bolder theory.

356
00:17:18,319 --> 00:17:22,720
He may go back to visit them.

357
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,079
He has to be disturbed.

358
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:27,799
A serial killer

359
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,160
like him

360
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:33,440
has a deep psychological void.

361
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,200
What kind of void?

362
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:37,880
In terms of relationships,

363
00:17:38,039 --> 00:17:39,200
he may live alone

364
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,960
after a painful romantic experience

365
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:43,119
in which he felt victimized.

366
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,160
Or his marriage may be failing,

367
00:17:46,319 --> 00:17:47,559
with serious conflict

368
00:17:47,839 --> 00:17:49,440
and likely separation.

369
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,000
He channels years of

370
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,839
repressed sexual frustration

371
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,480
into attacks

372
00:17:54,519 --> 00:17:56,680
on women he doesn't know.

373
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,039
If our theory is right,

374
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,039
he dumps the bodies

375
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,839
at one particular place

376
00:18:02,839 --> 00:18:04,440
in the sewer system.

377
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,000
Then he returns

378
00:18:07,079 --> 00:18:08,720
to admire his work,

379
00:18:09,119 --> 00:18:11,000
relive the crimes,

380
00:18:11,039 --> 00:18:13,400
and perhaps even handle the bodies.

381
00:18:13,799 --> 00:18:14,640
That could also mean

382
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:19,319
he may be an obsessive collector.

383
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,600
(Su Lin)

384
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,400
May I ask

385
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,559
do you know a student named Su Lin?

386
00:18:52,799 --> 00:18:53,480
You know her?

387
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:55,680
No.

388
00:19:04,039 --> 00:19:04,559
Mom.

389
00:19:05,039 --> 00:19:06,039
Do you have another hair tie?

390
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:06,599
Yes.

391
00:19:07,319 --> 00:19:07,960
Thick or thin?

392
00:19:08,319 --> 00:19:09,240
A thick one.

393
00:19:12,799 --> 00:19:13,240
Okay.

394
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,960
Didn't you tell me

395
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,680
at the school gate that day

396
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:20,160
that you didn't know Su Lin?

397
00:19:20,759 --> 00:19:22,000
Why do you have her costume?

398
00:19:24,319 --> 00:19:25,519
I don't know her.

399
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,359
We all share performance costumes.

400
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:30,640
We wear one today

401
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:31,640
and another tomorrow.

402
00:19:32,359 --> 00:19:34,920
I think there was a Su Lin before,

403
00:19:35,839 --> 00:19:37,640
but she later quit the team.

404
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,279
Mom, I have to go.

405
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:42,319
I'm heading to school.

406
00:19:42,359 --> 00:19:43,200
I have rehearsal tonight.

407
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,319
You're going this late?

408
00:19:44,559 --> 00:19:45,519
The contest is coming up.

409
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,200
Extra practice.

410
00:19:46,279 --> 00:19:47,039
I'd better go.

411
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:49,240
Be careful.

412
00:19:49,799 --> 00:19:50,720
Don't fall again.

413
00:19:54,559 --> 00:19:55,000
Jiang Ting.

414
00:19:57,599 --> 00:19:58,000
Here.

415
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:00,759
Mom never lets me drink soda.

416
00:20:02,359 --> 00:20:03,119
Don't misunderstand.

417
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:05,839
I only want to ask about Su Lin.

418
00:20:08,119 --> 00:20:09,839
Why do you keep asking about her?

419
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,240
You were in the same class.

420
00:20:14,599 --> 00:20:16,640
I just feel like

421
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:18,559
I let her down.

422
00:20:20,599 --> 00:20:24,119
Are you two really what Ma Na said?

423
00:20:24,559 --> 00:20:25,759
Don't listen to her nonsense.

424
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,440
She's never wanted for anything

425
00:20:27,839 --> 00:20:28,559
and only chases boys.

426
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:33,319
I heard Su Lin wanted to go to college,

427
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,400
so I recommended her

428
00:20:35,519 --> 00:20:36,519
for our recitation team.

429
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:39,720
Winning could add to her exam score.

430
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,440
Ma Na thought there was something

431
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,680
and made Su Lin miserable.

432
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:44,759
Then

433
00:20:46,079 --> 00:20:47,200
Su Lin disappeared.

434
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:49,519
Didn't she drop out?

435
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,640
That's what I thought at first.

436
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:54,599
But while I was

437
00:20:54,599 --> 00:20:55,880
sorting files for the teachers,

438
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,279
I heard them say

439
00:20:58,119 --> 00:21:00,039
her withdrawal was suspicious.

440
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,279
It made me wonder that

441
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,319
Ma Na's father has connections.

442
00:21:03,799 --> 00:21:05,200
What if he quietly...

443
00:21:05,319 --> 00:21:06,119
Don't say that.

444
00:21:11,319 --> 00:21:12,240
Besides,

445
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,400
this isn't something we can solve.

446
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,319
I still feel awful.

447
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,480
I keep replaying those days.

448
00:21:22,039 --> 00:21:23,200
What if I hadn't asked Su Lin

449
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,200
to join our recitation team?

450
00:21:25,119 --> 00:21:25,680
Or

451
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:27,519
what if I hadn't stepped in

452
00:21:27,559 --> 00:21:28,359
when they fought?

453
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,240
Impressive, Su Lin.

454
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:32,079
Stay away! Don't come closer!

455
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,160
I know what you mean.

456
00:21:37,799 --> 00:21:38,559
I understand.

457
00:21:40,119 --> 00:21:40,759
So

458
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,559
I want to do whatever I can,

459
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,160
even something small,

460
00:21:46,599 --> 00:21:49,440
so I won't feel quite as guilty.

461
00:21:50,519 --> 00:21:51,759
All I saw

462
00:21:51,799 --> 00:21:53,200
was Ma Na and the others around Su Lin.

463
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,400
Someone else may have seen more.

464
00:21:57,160 --> 00:22:00,160
I know this is hard for you too.

465
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:02,279
I even saw you

466
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,359
staring at one of Su Lin's books.

467
00:22:05,799 --> 00:22:06,319
I wasn't.

468
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:11,839
Is rehearsal about to start?

469
00:22:12,519 --> 00:22:13,519
We should go inside.

470
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:16,680
Tell me if you remember

471
00:22:16,759 --> 00:22:17,680
anything else.

472
00:22:21,559 --> 00:22:22,160
Don't run!

473
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:23,279
Na!

474
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:25,519
That's mine!

475
00:22:25,519 --> 00:22:27,200
The princess has arrived!

476
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,400
Hop off.

477
00:22:29,039 --> 00:22:29,960
You two...

478
00:22:33,359 --> 00:22:33,799
Na,

479
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:34,920
did your dad really hit you?

480
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:36,039
As if.

481
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:36,759
He wouldn't.

482
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:38,799
But

483
00:22:39,079 --> 00:22:40,519
who is Mr. Zhou's father-in-law,

484
00:22:40,599 --> 00:22:41,599
anyway?

485
00:22:41,759 --> 00:22:43,000
Even the principal fears him.

486
00:22:43,359 --> 00:22:44,200
Who cares?

487
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,559
He's just living off his wife.

488
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:46,880
I can't believe

489
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,359
he complained to the principal.

490
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:51,039
Why are you still watching TV?

491
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:53,319
Your dad will hit you when he's back.

492
00:22:53,359 --> 00:22:54,079
You know that.

493
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,720
Isn't Dad in the hospital?

494
00:22:56,359 --> 00:22:57,160
I wish.

495
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:58,839
Look at what we can afford.

496
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,440
You think we can pay for that?

497
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,400
But don't we have money now?

498
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:08,079
Enough.

499
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,400
Kids stay out of adult business.

500
00:23:09,839 --> 00:23:11,039
Go do your homework.

501
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,119
All you think about is TV.

502
00:23:12,279 --> 00:23:14,000
No one can control you.

503
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,920
He's not back yet.

504
00:23:17,279 --> 00:23:19,359
Just go do your homework.

505
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:21,839
Neither of you gives me any peace.

506
00:23:22,799 --> 00:23:24,200
Why is my life so hard?

507
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:32,960
Have you eaten?

508
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,400
Will this do?

509
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:40,920
It'll have to.

510
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:42,319
Here.

511
00:23:45,039 --> 00:23:45,960
Don't pour too much.

512
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,759
Tea shallow, wine full.

513
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:53,160
Here.

514
00:23:54,519 --> 00:23:55,079
Say a few words.

515
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:57,759
Say something.

516
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:03,160
Here's to our later years.

517
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:06,839
To good health. That's what matters.

518
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,640
Still no good with words.

519
00:24:09,839 --> 00:24:10,759
Slow down.

520
00:24:11,279 --> 00:24:12,680
It tastes sweet,

521
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,240
but it'll still get you drunk.

522
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,279
When have you ever seen me drunk?

523
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:19,559
That's true.

524
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,599
I never have.

525
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,960
Whenever you came over,

526
00:24:22,119 --> 00:24:23,519
you and Tai

527
00:24:23,599 --> 00:24:24,839
drank and bragged all night.

528
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:26,039
You never noticed me.

529
00:24:26,559 --> 00:24:28,319
He always got me talking.

530
00:24:28,599 --> 00:24:29,279
How corny.

531
00:24:31,279 --> 00:24:33,000
Back then, if not for Tai...

532
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:35,440
When a grenade fell by your feet,

533
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,119
he threw himself over it.

534
00:24:37,319 --> 00:24:39,039
He still carries six fragments.

535
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:40,680
You've told that story 800 times.

536
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:43,839
Eight thousand wouldn't be enough.

537
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,279
So you feel you owe him.

538
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,440
You never wanted to compete

539
00:24:48,519 --> 00:24:49,319
with him over anything.

540
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,200
I couldn't beat him.

541
00:24:52,119 --> 00:24:53,000
He was exceptional.

542
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,759
At our age,

543
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,519
we're past

544
00:25:10,559 --> 00:25:12,039
all that romance.

545
00:25:13,079 --> 00:25:14,400
We just want someone we know

546
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,160
and trust to share our lives with.

547
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,640
Isn't that enough?

548
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:20,480
Yes, it is.

549
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:24,640
Got it now?

550
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:27,160
Then this wine wasn't wasted.

551
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:29,200
Not completely.

552
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,519
But that Culture Center.

553
00:25:31,559 --> 00:25:32,720
I think I'll give it a try.

554
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,039
What class interests you?

555
00:25:35,119 --> 00:25:36,000
I'll help you choose.

556
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,839
What do you and Wu do there?

557
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:40,839
There you go again.

558
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:51,319
Class,

559
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,240
Ma Na brought us

560
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,359
an excellent tape.

561
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:57,039
I think it's perfect music

562
00:25:57,039 --> 00:25:59,400
for our English recitation practice.

563
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:00,920
So I've decided

564
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:03,319
we'll practice one extra hour today.

565
00:26:05,359 --> 00:26:06,519
Why are you groaning?

566
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:07,920
The contest is almost here.

567
00:26:08,119 --> 00:26:08,839
Let's push through.

568
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:10,039
Get ready.

569
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:20,960
Project your voices.

570
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:21,799
Louder. Come on.

571
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,519
(He tells everyone he's)

572
00:26:29,519 --> 00:26:30,640
(the bureau chief's son-in-law.)

573
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:31,880
(Bet he's completely useless.)

574
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,960
(Guys like him make me sick.)

575
00:26:34,039 --> 00:26:34,839
(He's worse than sick.)

576
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:35,839
(He's a total creep.)

577
00:26:35,839 --> 00:26:36,960
Are they talking about Mr. Zhou?

578
00:26:37,079 --> 00:26:37,519
Not me.

579
00:26:37,519 --> 00:26:38,079
(Did you know)

580
00:26:38,079 --> 00:26:39,680
(he writes poetry
at the Cultural Center?)

581
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:40,680
(No.)

582
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:43,640
(Love poems and all that.)

583
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:44,960
Who recorded this?

584
00:26:46,039 --> 00:26:47,079
(I know that poem.)

585
00:26:48,359 --> 00:26:49,240
Was it you?

586
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:51,920
Was it you?

587
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:53,480
(An ear of wheat? More like a potato.)

588
00:26:53,839 --> 00:26:54,799
(Then I must be a sweet potato.)

589
00:26:54,799 --> 00:26:55,440
Was it you?

590
00:26:55,759 --> 00:26:57,319
You took the tape last time.

591
00:26:58,240 --> 00:26:58,880
Gross, right?

592
00:26:59,039 --> 00:26:59,680
Who did this?

593
00:26:59,839 --> 00:27:01,400
Who secretly recorded us?

594
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:02,039
(Soup dumpling.)

595
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:14,640
No, it wasn't...

596
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:15,799
Mr. Zhou,

597
00:27:16,599 --> 00:27:17,000
I...

598
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,480
I...

599
00:27:29,599 --> 00:27:30,440
Badmouthing people

600
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,119
is a bad habit.

601
00:27:33,559 --> 00:27:34,160
I...

602
00:27:43,599 --> 00:27:44,559
Let's go. Class is over.

603
00:27:44,799 --> 00:27:45,440
Yeah.

604
00:27:46,279 --> 00:27:47,519
Who had the nerve?

605
00:27:47,759 --> 00:27:48,720
Who did it?

606
00:27:49,559 --> 00:27:50,640
That was way out of line.

607
00:27:54,119 --> 00:27:55,000
Who cares?

608
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,279
He's just living off his wife.

609
00:27:56,559 --> 00:27:57,519
I can't believe

610
00:27:57,599 --> 00:27:59,000
he complained to the principal.

611
00:27:59,240 --> 00:27:59,839
But

612
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:01,559
who is Mr. Zhou's father-in-law,

613
00:28:01,599 --> 00:28:02,680
anyway?

614
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:06,319
Jiang Ting.

615
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,079
You're still here?

616
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:11,359
I helped Mr. Zhou move some things.

617
00:28:12,559 --> 00:28:13,880
That trick just now was brilliant.

618
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:14,839
The recording.

619
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:15,880
That was so clever.

620
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:17,880
It felt good too.

621
00:28:20,599 --> 00:28:21,680
I'd better go.

622
00:28:22,079 --> 00:28:22,519
Bye.

623
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,599
Maybe it was Su Lin.

624
00:29:16,359 --> 00:29:17,079
Please.

625
00:29:18,359 --> 00:29:19,559
Please let me go.

626
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,640
I'm begging you.

627
00:29:26,759 --> 00:29:27,400
Please.

628
00:29:34,279 --> 00:29:34,799
Please.

629
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,359
My mom is waiting for me.

630
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,839
My dad is waiting too.

631
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,480
I have a little brother at home.

632
00:29:41,119 --> 00:29:42,200
They're all waiting for me.

633
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:45,279
Please.

634
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:47,240
Please let me go home.

635
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:49,440
I want to go home.

636
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:51,039
Please.

637
00:29:51,799 --> 00:29:53,079
Please let me leave.

638
00:29:55,839 --> 00:29:56,440
Please.

639
00:30:00,119 --> 00:30:01,440
Let me go home, please.

640
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:43,599
Help!

641
00:32:43,759 --> 00:32:45,359
Someone help me!

642
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:46,480
Help!

643
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:56,680
♪Darkness spreads like ink♪

644
00:32:56,960 --> 00:33:03,720
♪Lost eyes search the shadows♪

645
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:11,000
♪So many stories hide in life's corners♪

646
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:16,360
♪I remember every joy and sorrow♪

647
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:20,440
♪Till a dazzling beam breaks through♪

648
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:23,520
♪I know that light is salvation♪

649
00:33:23,760 --> 00:33:26,920
♪The torn night declares an end♪

650
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:30,880
♪And loneliness fades into nothing♪

651
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:37,120
♪I'll fight free of the darkness♪

652
00:33:37,600 --> 00:33:41,000
♪And break the chains of fate♪

653
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:45,120
♪Let me touch the blue sky above♪

654
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:51,400
♪That light suddenly falls♪

655
00:33:51,640 --> 00:33:57,360
♪Saving all my broken pieces♪

656
00:34:32,200 --> 00:34:38,960
♪So many stories hide in life's corners♪

657
00:34:39,200 --> 00:34:44,600
♪I remember every joy and sorrow♪

658
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:48,640
♪Till a dazzling beam breaks through♪

659
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:51,720
♪I know that light is salvation♪

660
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:55,160
♪The torn night declares an end♪

661
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:59,080
♪And loneliness fades into nothing♪

662
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:05,360
♪I'll fight free of the darkness♪

663
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:09,200
♪And break the chains of fate♪

664
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:13,320
♪Let me touch the blue sky above♪

665
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:19,600
♪That light suddenly falls♪

666
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:23,320
♪Saving all my broken pieces♪

667
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:34,200
♪It saves me♪

668
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:17,239
Why are you here?

669
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,559
Shouldn't you be in class?

670
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,039
Don't even ask.

671
00:36:30,519 --> 00:36:32,280
Everyone else is seven or eight.

672
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,159
I'm ten.

673
00:36:33,159 --> 00:36:34,440
I'm a head taller than them.

674
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:37,360
They call me a gorilla or baboon,

675
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:38,119
a big dumb oaf.

676
00:36:38,519 --> 00:36:39,960
They can keep that stupid school.

677
00:36:40,239 --> 00:36:41,800
You're bigger than they are.

678
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:44,440
You're Vincent

679
00:36:45,519 --> 00:36:47,039
from Beauty and the Beast.

680
00:36:48,119 --> 00:36:49,800
You should be stronger than them.

681
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,119
You're giving up already?

682
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:54,519
They're just little brats.

683
00:36:55,159 --> 00:36:56,800
I can't be bothered.

684
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:02,280
Are you full?

685
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:04,239
I can fry two more.

686
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:06,639
I'm full.

687
00:37:07,039 --> 00:37:08,400
I like the crispy egg bits.

688
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:09,320
Crispy and delicious.

689
00:37:14,719 --> 00:37:16,320
Why haven't I seen your sister lately?

690
00:37:16,639 --> 00:37:18,159
She's staying with our uncle.

691
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:19,920
She'll take the exam there.

692
00:37:22,199 --> 00:37:23,360
It's been a while.

693
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,519
Has she called home?

694
00:37:31,079 --> 00:37:31,719
Mr. Gu,

695
00:37:35,079 --> 00:37:36,639
what do I do? I miss my sister.

696
00:38:52,320 --> 00:38:53,239
I'll beat you!

697
00:38:56,760 --> 00:38:57,559
Don't really hit him!

698
00:38:57,559 --> 00:38:58,719
You worthless little brat!

699
00:38:58,840 --> 00:39:02,719
I sold your sister to put you in school!

700
00:39:03,199 --> 00:39:04,920
You ungrateful brat!

701
00:39:05,159 --> 00:39:06,880
Don't actually hit him!

702
00:39:07,159 --> 00:39:07,719
What's going on?

703
00:39:08,039 --> 00:39:10,320
If your teacher hadn't called,

704
00:39:10,599 --> 00:39:12,239
I'd have thought you'd improved.

705
00:39:12,639 --> 00:39:13,960
Don't hit him!

706
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,039
I'm not hitting you.

707
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:16,440
Come here.

708
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:18,920
Come on.

709
00:39:21,840 --> 00:39:23,199
You'd better remember this.

710
00:39:24,559 --> 00:39:27,480
Only if your sister is dead

711
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:29,880
can you get registered,

712
00:39:32,599 --> 00:39:34,000
go to school,

713
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:36,440
and leave this family

714
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:37,639
to make a life for yourself.

715
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:40,079
You don't have a sister anymore.

716
00:39:40,679 --> 00:39:43,719
I don't need registration!

717
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:46,559
I want my sister!

718
00:39:48,039 --> 00:39:50,440
We already sold her.

719
00:39:52,559 --> 00:39:53,880
As long as she's around,

720
00:39:53,960 --> 00:39:55,519
this family has no future.

721
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,079
Do you understand?

722
00:39:58,079 --> 00:40:00,000
I want my sister!

723
00:40:00,079 --> 00:40:01,519
Your sister is dead.

724
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:06,679
I want my sister!

725
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:10,239
She's never coming back.

726
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,400
Do you hear me?

727
00:40:11,599 --> 00:40:13,239
You're lying!

728
00:40:14,880 --> 00:40:16,559
You're all lying!

729
00:41:24,200 --> 00:41:26,560
(Have you ever felt)

730
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:31,000
(the whole world suddenly go empty?)

731
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:32,960
(Su Lin's Diary)

732
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:39,520
=Ren Yu=
(Next Time...)

733
00:41:39,639 --> 00:41:41,199
Weren't you looking

734
00:41:41,199 --> 00:41:42,639
for the child who helped someone?

735
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:43,599
Found her?

736
00:41:47,559 --> 00:41:49,159
Did you get along with Su Lin?

737
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,320
Who's Su Lin?

738
00:41:53,519 --> 00:41:54,760
Your classmate, Su Lin.

739
00:41:54,760 --> 00:41:55,519
You don't know her?

740
00:41:57,039 --> 00:41:59,480
He asked if you knew Su Lin's dad.

741
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:05,039
Remember your promise.

742
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:08,440
I only have one son.

743
00:42:09,119 --> 00:42:09,800
I have no daughter.

744
00:42:39,200 --> 00:42:42,160
♪Never loud, never surging♪

745
00:42:45,560 --> 00:42:48,480
♪I gather my worries and build a wall♪

746
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:52,840
♪Around me♪

747
00:42:54,360 --> 00:43:00,080
♪By my pillow, I hear a dark fairy tale♪

748
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:13,720
♪One burst of pain, a thousand blooms♪

749
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:24,440
♪Now I stand with myself♪

750
00:43:24,680 --> 00:43:28,720
♪Each becomes the other's shore♪

751
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:06,000
♪By my pillow, I hear a dark fairy tale♪

752
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:19,160
♪One burst of pain, a thousand blooms♪

753
00:44:24,480 --> 00:44:30,800
♪The struggle inside the silence♪

754
00:44:31,120 --> 00:44:37,880
♪Who can hear it?♪
